tor $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|1-2|+|4-5|+|-2-3| \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1069 "q-254851" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $a=[2,\\,6]^{T}$ and $b=[5,\\,3]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55bdf128-1307-57a2-a09e-523ed9c58971" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518140 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|2-5{|}^{2}+|6-3{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & ≈4.243.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1069 "q-254909" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $a=[7,\\,6,\\,-2]^{T}$ and $b=[-1,\\,2,\\,4]^{T}.$ Find the Chebyshev distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78d962fb-98a1-54a9-be40-612e78bd3a7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518161 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty }\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{\\infty }=max(|{v}_{1}|,|{v}_{2}|,…,|{v}_{N}|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =max(|7-(-1)|,|6-2|,|-2-4|) \\\\  & =max(8,4,6) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1069 "q-254915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $a=[0,\\,-6]^{T}$ and $b=[0.5,\\,-7]^{T}.$ Find the Chebyshev distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79a48270-e1b9-5009-9c26-f6b63d86b07c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518162 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty }\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{\\infty }=max(|{v}_{1}|,|{v}_{2}|,…,|{v}_{N}|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0.5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =max(|0-0.5|,|-6-(-7)|) \\\\  & =max(0.5,1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-254910" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518163 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518163 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $a=[-3,\\,5,\\,1]^{T}$ and $b=[2,\\,7,\\,4]^{T}.$ Find the Chebyshev distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518163 #edb/ref 1072